invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_mul.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: a digit reads one bit fewer than its window holds, so its size
  loses its top bit and every digit whose window has that bit set names
  an entry half its size: about half the windows of a random scalar are
  wrong, at both widths. bin/p256_equiv_test holds both multiplications to
  the 32-bit files on edge and random scalars.

--- old
    for (size_t t = 1; t < bits; t++) {
--- new
    for (size_t t = 1; t < bits - 1; t++) {
